  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'BALANCE ON A REAL FLOATING LOG

    Two to four trucks, first to five
    round wins. One human can practise against AI; any human/AI mixture and fully
    autonomous matches are supported. Drive, steer, brake before reversing, reposition
    your weight and physically bump opponents.


    Fresh ACTION braces for0.85seconds,
    lowering your center of mass and applying real wheel braking; then2.6seconds
    cooldown. It cannot rescue a truck already in the water. NWH wheels and PhysX
    contacts determine movement; the owned Floating Entities solver supplies the
    log''s buoyancy. Realistic mass scaling applies uniformly to the trucks'' wheels/suspension/torque
    in this mode. No invisible balancing platform or extra collision impulse.


    A
    genuine chassis fall into the water eliminates; minor wheel overhang alone never
    does. The final survivor wins. Batch all falls from one physics step: simultaneous
    final falls draw and replay. From35seconds waves build gradually; a120second
    unresolved heat is an explicit draw and replay. Starts rotate each round. Recorded
    actual log/truck motion offers angles, slow/fast, rewind and skip. Pause/reconnect
    preserves current bodies, round and score. Shared settings and rematch configuration
    apply. Offline only.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
